            <ArticleTitle>[Lesions of the cauda equina after dimer-X myelography (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>216-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe five cases of an uncommon complication after Dimer X Myelography consisting in a more or less complete lesion of the caudia equina. Up to the present only seven similar cases have been reported in the literature. The evolution and the clinical symptoms of these cases were similar to those reported by others. While in the cases presented the clinical outcome was favourable, with complete recovery in all cases, less favourable evolutions with definitive neurological symptoms are described by others.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
